This session's work touched two of the 13 issues, so I replied on those two and left the rest alone.

• #1252: commented and closed. It's fixed in c1205469. The yoyo agents header no longer says "not yet used by yoyo". It now says which agents the model can actually delegate to with the agent tool. The pinned test checks the new wording. The same commit makes a definition's maxTurns actually limit the child's turns (it used to be ignored), and an agent file with maxTurns: 0 is now skipped with a reason instead of loading. The listing also says plainly that a definition's own model isn't used yet. That part stays open on #1250.
